\help opens the help file of a command. Write the command
with its backslash as the argument:

\help \tempo

By default the help file replaces the text of the current
pane. Your text is not lost: close the help file with
Ctrl+W followed by q (Ctrl+W alone in insert mode, or
:q) and the pane gets its text back.

To open the help file in a new pane instead, add vert or
hor as a second argument:

\help \tempo vert

\help \tempo hor

vert splits the window vertically and hor splits it
horizontally, like the keyboard shortcuts for new panes.

If no help file exists for the command, you get the error
"couldn't find help file for" followed by the command,
and the new pane, if any, is closed. \help alone gives
the error "nothing specified to open its help file".
